meta {
  name: Get Current User
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  # Get Current Authenticated User

  Retrieve the current user's profile using their access token.

  ## Authentication Required
  - Yes (Bearer token)

  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "id": 1,
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "username": "johndoe",
    "first_name": "John",
    "last_name": "Doe",
    "bio": "Travel enthusiast",
    "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/...",
    "email_verified": true,
    "is_active": true,
    "default_currency": "USD",
    "date_format": "YYYY-MM-DD",
    "timezone": "UTC",
    "language": "en",
    "created_at": "2024-11-08T12:00:00",
    "last_login_at": "2024-11-08T12:30:00"
  }
  ```

  ## Use Cases
  - Verify that authentication is working
  - Get user info after login
  - Check which user is currently authenticated
  - Same as GET /users/me but in auth context

  ## Error Responses
  - **401 Unauthorized**: No token or invalid token
  - **403 Forbidden**: User is inactive or deleted
  - **404 Not Found**: User not found in database
}
